course: dictionary
lesson: 5280
title: Juggling with words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Juggle has two meanings. The first is keeping several objects moving in the air by throwing and catching them. The second is dealing with several jobs or activities at the same time. The words around it show you which meaning is meant.
explain: «Asian small-clawed otters juggle pebbles with their paws.» Pebbles are small stones and paws are animal feet, so the otters are tossing stones around. That is the first meaning. Swap it in: "keeping pebbles moving by tossing them" still makes sense.
explain: Now try the second meaning: «Grown-ups juggle work and family.» Nobody is throwing anything here. The clues are work and family, so juggle means managing both at once. Check it: "managing work and family at the same time" fits the sentence, so it is right.
fact: Juggle is a verb: juggle, juggles, juggled, juggling.
fact: «Juggle» means to keep several objects moving in the air by throwing and catching them over and over.
fact: «Juggle» can also mean to try to deal with several jobs or activities at the same time.
fact: Phrases you may hear are juggle three balls and juggle things.
fact: «Asian small-clawed otters, the smallest otters in the world, juggle pebbles with their paws, perhaps as play or practice for handling food.»
exercise: «Asian small-clawed otters juggle pebbles with their paws.» What does juggle mean here? | Drop pebbles into the water | *Keep pebbles moving by tossing and catching them | Sort pebbles by size | Hide pebbles in a pocket
exercise: Mum says, «I have to juggle work and homework tonight.» What does juggle mean? | To stop working completely | *To deal with several jobs at the same time | To lose track of time | To throw and catch objects
exercise: Which phrase is about keeping objects moving in the air? | juggle work and family | *juggle three balls | juggle a plan | juggle the time
test: Pupils juggle homework and clubs. Which meaning fits? | *Deal with homework and clubs at the same time | Throw homework and clubs in the air | Sort homework and clubs into two piles | Forget about homework and clubs
test: Which word is the past tense of juggle? | juggling | *juggled | juggle | juggles
exam: Which sentence uses juggle to mean keeping objects in the air? | Jo tries to juggle her plans with her friends | *Rosa can juggle three balls at once | Dad has to juggle the bills and the bus times | Sam will juggle his clubs and his homework this week
